Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0379: leaderboard native addon built and verified
 (Windows pending)

Doc-only -- no game-repo code changed yet, deliberately. Records real,
verified progress on the custom leaderboard addon (steamworks.js fork,
not a separate module -- avoids a real double-SteamAPI_Init() risk
confirmed via search). Compiles clean against the fork's real pinned
steamworks-rs revision, a genuine Linux .node build exists via the real
napi build toolchain, nm confirms it's wired to the real Steam API
leaderboard functions. Not wired into electron/main.ts yet: doing so
before a Windows build exists would break achievements/DLC on Windows
too (index.js's platform loader has no fallback, and require() happens
at module-import time before any try/catch runs), not just leave
leaderboards unavailable there. Fork + Linux build + integration
instructions handed over separately (steamworks-leaderboard-fork.zip),
not committed into this repo -- it's a dependency, not part of
Guildbound's own source, same as the plain npm steamworks.js package
already is.
